+The table shows the highest completed integer match in each chain, not a failure threshold. All 33 completed full-pool MIPs match their targets and prove their fleets optimal within their saved pools. Their CG runs have pricing certificates, and individual-route replay passed. These are covering runs with 240 kWh batteries and 240 kW charging; shared charger capacity and return-SOC constraints are absent. Duplicate-trip removal was not validated. Higher k values remain in progress. “Earlier 512-route buses” is the earlier result when at most 512 saved routes were inherited. Chain 2 k14 uses its recorded shutdown-repaired retry. Later chain pools differ, so this table does not isolate a single code change.
 
 The initial comparisons—C3 k11, C4 k10 and C6 k11—used identical saved parent pools in both treatments and reached the same certified LP objectives within 1e-8. Full inheritance retained about 34,000–41,000 routes in 2.4–3.3 minutes. C4 k10 isolates a pool limitation: the old pool was proved to require 11 buses; the new pool provides 10\. C3 k11’s old 12-bus result was unproved, so MIP search difficulty may also matter there. CG times throughout this section use existing graph caches; original graph construction is excluded.
 
